      <title>Great Valley ousted by Upper Darby in first round</title>
      <link>https://www.dailylocal.com/2026/02/14/great-valley-ousted-by-upper-darby-in-first-round/</link>
      <description>EAST WHITELAND — They say the race is usually won by the team that gets out of the gate fast. That axiom could apply to Friday night’s opening round District 1 6A boys basketball contest between Upper Darby and host Great Valley. The 18th-seeded Royals scored the first 19 points of the game en route to a 58-48 win over the No. 15 Patriots. The win puts Upper Darby (13-10) into the second round Tuesday against Methacton. The Patriots end their season at 17-7. Upper Darby shot a torrid 62 percent</description>
